cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use scicomm, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "scicomm: Assess Fidelity and Audience Fit in Science Communication"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-02
authors:
  - family-names: "Sánchez-Núñez"
    given-names: "Pablo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7845-9506"
url: "https://pablosancheznunez.com/scicomm/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pablosancheznunez/scicomm"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - science communication
  - readability
  - exaggeration
  - uncertainty
  - plain language
  - Spanish
  - R
abstract: >-
  An R package that describes a scientific finding once and checks each text
  that communicates it to specialists, students or the public: fidelity to
  the evidence (causal language, numbers, population, limitations,
  certainty), clarity, accessibility and uncertainty, in English and Spanish.
